<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Structure-Shaped Convention

Structure-Shaped Convention names a mechanism that ''wears structure's clothes over an agreement''.

The node reaches for a structural cure — correctly, because the house holds that a baked-in answer beats a documented one, and that a cure by subtraction beats a cure by disclaimer. Then it builds a mechanism whose guarantee ''rides a register the substrate cannot enforce'', and reports the property as won. The failure hides in the register-jump, never in the mechanism: every step reads sound, and the guarantee simply never lands anywhere that can hold it.

''The tell'': the node can name WHAT the mechanism forbids and cannot name WHAT ENFORCES the forbidding.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/instances>>

!! Two instances, one arc, both caught from outside

''① THE COMPOSITION REFUSAL.'' A design proposed that a cap-stack composing both the declare-cap and the gauge-cap FAIL TO COMPOSE — //the naming layer must never certify//, turned from prose into a build error. Outside research returned the register-jump: the refusal gates ''self-review'' and touches none of self-interest, advocacy, familiarity or intimidation. Across seven canonical failures in a field that formalised the separation for a century, ''six kept structural separation perfectly and failed anyway'' — because ''whoever pays the gauge bends the gauge''. A control over one threat class, reported as a control over the relation.

''② THE UN-COERCIBLE ABSENCE.'' A design proposed a typed absence a caller could not mistake for an answer. Outside research returned the register-jump twice over: the property holds ''at compile time only'', on a checker whose published charter declines soundness as a goal — and a forged value arriving off the wire typechecks as a seated reading. The guarantee named a runtime property and lived in a layer that evaporates before runtime.

''The shared shape'': in both, the mechanism sat one register ABOVE what could enforce it — a composition rule above an economic relation, a static type above a wire. ''Neither was wrong. Both were reported as more than they were.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-law>>

!! The law

> ''A mechanism MUST name the substrate that enforces it, and the node MUST ask what can seize or bypass that substrate.''

An unenforceable guarantee costs more than an honest convention, because a convention keeps its human floor and a false structure retires one. `structural, not conventional` MUST NOT become //we deleted the convention//.

''The recovery runs in three moves'':

# ''Name the enforcing substrate.'' Cryptography · arity · uninhabited types · a module boundary · an economic relation · a published record. If nothing gets named, the guarantee has not landed.
# ''Ask who can seize it.'' The party holding the measuring instrument takes the frame regardless of governance design; a static type surrenders at the wire; a composition rule surrenders to whoever funds both sides.
# ''Demote or re-seat.'' Either move the guarantee down to a substrate that holds it, or ''restate it as a convention and keep the human floor beside it'' — a challenge channel, a standing to object, a named party who may raise the discrepancy.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-diagnostic>>

!! Why the node cannot catch this alone

Both instances arrived from OUTSIDE — a field that had already run the experiment for a century, and a literature that had already named the failure modes. ''Neither came from noticing.'' The mechanism reads sound from inside because the register-jump happens in the same breath as the design, and re-reading the design re-enacts the jump.

That makes this a ''sibling of Confabulation-as-Canon'' rather than a variant: there the node's own naming read back as evidence; here the node's own mechanism reads back as enforcement. Both cure the same way — ''route the certification outside the turn''.

<<~/ahu>>

